                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Review as of 16-Apr-2022 [/h1]\n\n[h1] Intro [/h1]\nAn interesting puzzle solving platformer \n\n[h1] What I like [/h1]\n- Can be done in 1 run\n- Alot of secrets to be unlock\n- Puzzles are ranging from beginner to intermediate\n- [spoiler] interesting concept of reversing time [/spoiler]\n- I like the setting of the story and how the protag's involvement is\n- [spoiler] Ending does indicate as though there's a second game, or more chapters [/spoiler]\n\n[h1] What I don't like [/h1]\n- there's not much communication between the devs and community in discuession\n- There's bugs where on the audio settings\n- The starting of the game there's vocals reading the game but it just didn't continue when heading to later chapter\n- The story speed was too fast to be read and can't be change\n- For the way how the puzzle proceeded and planned, [spoiler] the last boss is too easy. like really really too easy for it to be a boss. the patterns are really repetitive and no challenge to it, The stages puzzle were much better designed than the boss stage.  [/spoiler]\n\n[h1] Others [/h1]\n- stream wise, game was stream on twitch.tv/execell_is_here\n- there's an issue with the game category as it share the same name as another game.\n- i normally recommend games but with the issues on the bugs at this point, and also the lack of responses from the game devs, it really feels, in my humble opinion, the game devs isn't taking the community seriously in regards to bugs and responses. I dont feel right recommending the game as it is now.",
